# Financial News Sentiment Classification

A machine learning project that classifies financial news headlines into **Positive, Negative, and Neutral** sentiment categories using Natural Language Processing (NLP).

### Dataset
- **File:** `all-data.csv`
- **Input:** Financial news text
- **Target:** Sentiment label

### Techniques Used
- Text preprocessing using NLTK
- Stopword removal and Snowball Stemming
- TF-IDF feature extraction
- Logistic Regression classification
- Hyperparameter tuning using GridSearchCV
- Model evaluation using accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score

### Initial Results
- **Accuracy:** 70.9%
- **Macro F1-score:** 0.59
- **Train-test split:** 80:20

*Initial results were obtained using Multinomial Naive Bayes. The Logistic Regression model is being optimized and evaluated separately.*

### Learning Outcomes
- Text preprocessing and feature engineering
- Building an NLP classification pipeline
- Handling imbalanced sentiment classes
- Evaluating machine learning models

### Future Improvements
- Compare different preprocessing techniques and classifiers
- Improve performance across all sentiment classes
- Deploy the model using FastAPI and build a React frontend
